Assembly    Interpolated
SourceFiles main stats

# sip (short for string interpolation) is a metaprogram that i use in my own projects.
# it rewrites string-interpolated printf("{x}") calls into the
# plain printf("%d", x) form before the compiler ever sees the file.
# The whole tool lives in this folder and is built first as a dependency,
# the hook then runs the freshly built exe over this module's sources,
# right before compilation. RiftBuild appends every source
# file's full path to the command.

Depend sip/

PreCompileAllFiles.Exec "sip/Build/sip.exe"

# The per-file flavor launches the tool once per source file instead,
# with that file's path appended last - same idea, one file at a time:
#
#   PreCompileFile.Exec "sip/Build/sip.exe"

# SourceFiles above matters here: without the whitelist, recursive source
# discovery would try to compile the tool's own sources into this module.

Assert.Platform windows
